# Who painted it? Match four famous paintings
subtitle: "Match the Mona Lisa, The Starry Night, The Scream and Girl with a Pearl Earring to their painters, and hear how a theft made one world-famous."

## Who painted it? Match four famous paintings
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: loc
      title: 'Theft of Mona Lisa: Topics in Chronicling America'
      authors: Library of Congress
      year: 2023
      url: https://guides.loc.gov/chronicling-america-theft-mona-lisa
      finding: stolen from the Louvre on 21 August 1911 by Vincenzo Peruggia, recovered in Florence in December 1913; newspaper coverage made it world-famous

    cards art size 1.25 hidden true
        * "Mona Lisa" icon.of "framed picture" icon.set twemoji match Leonardo
        * "The Starry Night" icon.of "night with stars" icon.set twemoji match "Van Gogh"
        * "The Scream" icon.of "face screaming in fear" icon.set twemoji match Munch
        * "Girl with a Pearl Earring" icon.of girl icon.set twemoji match Vermeer
    text s1911 "stolen 1911" #b5482e cites ["loc"] x 200 y 470 font_size 40 hidden true
    text s1913 "found 1913" #2f6b8f cites ["loc"] x 800 y 470 font_size 40 hidden true
    path fr_o closed #8a5a2b points [[356,286],[644,286],[644,638],[356,638]] style.stroke_width 9 hidden true
    path fr_i closed #8a5a2b points [[385,315],[615,315],[615,609],[385,609]] style.stroke_width 2 hidden true
    ellipse ml_head #5b4a2e x 500 y 502 rx 42 ry 54 style.fill #d9b26b style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.6 hidden true
    path ml_hair smooth #3d3833 points [[439,366],[446,462],[465,542],[500,566],[535,542],[554,462],[561,366]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    path ml_body smooth #3d3833 points [[404,321],[428,390],[500,430],[572,390],[596,321]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    group mona members ["ml_head","ml_hair","ml_body"] hidden true
    group empty members ["fr_o","fr_i"] hidden true

    card title "Who painted it?"

Four of the most famous paintings in the world. But who painted which?
    draw art

    ask "Match each painting to its painter: drag from one card to its partner." on art store m feedback.style warm feedback.perfect "The museum guards would hire you." feedback.good "A good eye for a brushstroke." feedback.poor "Even gallery visitors mix these up." feedback.none "Now you can stroll the galleries knowing four more."
        right: All {m} right.
        wrong: {m} right. Here are the true pairs.

Van Gogh painted The Starry Night in 1889, from the view out of his room at an asylum in the south of France.
    highlight art_2 art_m_2

Munch made The Scream in several versions, in paint and in pastel.
    highlight art_3 art_m_3

And Vermeer's girl may be no portrait at all, but a study of a face in a fancy costume.
    highlight art_4 art_m_4

But the most famous of them all was not always so famous.
    highlight art_1 art_m_1

    erase art

In August 1911, a former Louvre worker, Vincenzo Peruggia, walked out with the Mona Lisa under his smock.
    draw s1911 empty

Newspapers around the world printed her face, and crowds queued to stare at the empty wall.
    highlight s1911

Two years later Peruggia tried to sell her in Florence, and was caught.
    draw s1913

    draw mona

She came home to Paris more famous than ever. The theft made her the world's best-known painting.
    text famous "most famous" #b5482e x 500 y 232 font_size 44
---
